      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5fca5df4d58780532024a52b|full_name}: A common point of failure in VR controllers is the analog stick. I can access expression via the wings of the quick menu, but I cannot access the mirror options. When I need to use the mirror settings, I have to struggle to get to it and actually hit the right options.\nThe old portable mirror mod had both a quick menu option as well as integration into the action menu. The default was the quick menu; which allows quick, direct, and intentional access. I would prefer this.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-08-11T02:50:16.630Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "As it stands, VRChat is expanding the number of features and options available to users. However, many features are beginning to enter the Action Menu unnecessarily, which causes confusion, bloat, and makes accessibility of regular features more frustrating.\nAt the same time, **the Camera menu is mostly barren**, and would provide a fitting space for toggling such an option as the Personal Mirror.\n \n# Design & Implementation\n- The camera menu will be renamed to \"Cameras & More\"\n- The Personal Mirror, Face Mirror, & Calibration Mirror toggles will be moved to the \"Cameras & More\" menu, under the collapsable subheading \"Mirrors\"\n- When the mirror is held, a radial menu similar to the Action Menu will be displayed, containing the mirror's various options.\n- Alternatively, a collapsable menu bar, similar to the Selfie Camera, may also be displayed to the side of the mirror, for operation when unheld.\n- Instead of a radial menu, [Joystick operation of the collapsable menu bar](https://feedback.vrchat.com/feature-requests/p/accessibility-offer-optional-joystick-navigation-of-menus) could be utilized.",
  "error": null,
